\pard\sl-240\slmult1 \cf1\lang1033\fs24\f0 Castle Quest\par
\cf2 by Andrew Cornish\par
\par
You've heard rumours that great treasure is hidden inside Castle Oggleboggle, and you intend to find it. The castle is full of deadly traps, but it's worth the risk for the incredible treasure that awaits you. Wearing a sweatshirt and a pair of trousers, you march up to the castle and prepare to begin your quest.\par
\par
You are outside the castle. The castle entrance is to the north. The small rock is also here.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are in the castle's main hallway. There are doors in the north, east and west walls. The south door leads outside. There is a wooden chair halfway along the hall.  Also here is the 'welcome' mat.\par
\cf1 \par
west\par
\cf2 You move west.\par
This is the castle kitchen. In the middle of the room stands a stove. There are doors in the north and south walls. The east door leads back to the main hallway.  Also here is the human brain.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
This is King Thingalot's private study. In the middle of the room stand a bronze table and a bronze chair. On the north wall is a green button. A door to the south leads back to the kitchen.  Also here is the book.\par
\cf1 \par
press green button\par
\cf2 The green button has been pressed. Well done - that was something you had to do. Now you can go through the north door in the main hallway.\par
\cf1 \par
south\par
\cf2 You move south.\par
This is the castle kitchen. In the middle of the room stands a stove. There are doors in the north and south walls. The east door leads back to the main hallway.  Also here is the human brain.\par
\cf1 \par
east\par
\cf2 You move east.\par
You are in the castle's main hallway. There are doors in the north, east and west walls. The south door leads outside. There is a wooden chair halfway along the hall.  Also here is the 'welcome' mat.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You now stand in the castle dining room. A large table stands in the middle of the room. There is a door in the north wall. The south door leads back to the main hallway.  Also here is the human lung.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are in the castle gallery. However, there is only one painting here. There are doors in the north and west walls. To the east, there is a hall lined with brass. The south door leads back to the dining room.\par
\cf1 \par
east\par
\cf2 You move east.\par
You now stand in the Brass Hall. To the east, a heavy iron portcullis blocks the way. Next to it are a blue lever and a black lever. One of these levers must be for raising the portcullis. The west door leads back to the gallery.\par
\cf1 \par
pull blue lever\par
\cf2 As you pull the blue lever, the heavy iron portcullis slowly rises into the ceiling. Well done - that was something you had to do. Now you can proceed east.\par
\cf1 \par
east\par
\cf2 You move east.\par
This room is circular. There are doors in the north, south and east doors. The Brass Hall is to the west.\par
\cf1 \par
south\par
\cf2 You move south.\par
You are now standing on a balcony outside the castle. There are two floorplates here, one red and one white. These floorplates are switches, and you must stand on one of them. The north door leads back to the circular room inside the castle.  Also here is the beef sausage.\par
\cf1 \par
stand on red floorplate\par
\cf2 When you stand on the red floorplate, it sinks into the floor. Well done - that was something you had to do. Now you can go through the east door in the circular room.\par
\cf1 \par
north\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
This room is circular. There are doors in the north, south and east doors. The Brass Hall is to the west.\par
\cf1 \par
east\par
\cf2 You move east.\par
This is the puzzle room. As you enter, the door slams shut behind you and locks itself! Now you cannot retrace your steps. A disembodied voice booms, "I must congratulate you on getting this far, adventurer. To continue, you must answer this question. What is two to the power of three? The answer is either six or eight." When you have made your decision, type in your answer.\par
\cf1 \par
eight\par
\cf2 You have answered correctly! Suddenly, you feel a strange tingling sensation and your vision blurs. A second later, you find yourself in a triangular room, which will be described next. Well done!  This is the treasure room. Sitting on the ground is a treasure chest. It's open and you can see the treasure inside - gems, gold coins and gold bars. You can hardly believe it - you've found the treasure!  Also here is the hamburger.\par
